# Line ends

# The files of the programs and datasets converted from CK, their licence texts and the patches are kept
# byte for byte, as CK had them and as they were tested (some sources have Windows line ends): no
# conversion when they are committed or checked out, whatever core.autocrlf says. A program's input
# with other line ends would give other outputs.
program/*/src/** -text
dataset/*/files/** -text
task/import-ck/files/licenses/** -text
task/import-ck/files/patches/** -text

# Scripts: CRLF for cmd.exe (it can misread the labels of a batch file with LF line ends), LF for sh
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
